{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>From the heavens</b> — Because he mentioned the might of HaShem, he said that He knows the secrets of the heart, and behold He is wise and mighty. And the meaning of \"looked down\" is as though He sees everything with His eyes." "And he mentioned the heavens — because they surround all the earth." "And he said: <b>all the inhabitants of</b> — that He will not overlook any person among them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:22.010688171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}